# Rime Dryad can be blocked through an ordinary Forest, but cannot be blocked once the defending player controls a snow Forest (CR 702.14c).
[Bot1 Deck]
Rime Dryad
Mox Emerald
Memnite
Forest x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Snow-Covered Forest
Ornithopter
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rime Dryad.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Rime Dryad > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Rime Dryad)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Snow-Covered Forest.Play
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Rime Dryad > Bot2; Memnite > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Rime Dryad)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Memnite)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Rime Dryad.Power = 1
